# graphify corpus exclusions (gitignore syntax)
#
# graphify's built-in SKIP_DIRS covers node_modules/.git/dist/build/coverage,
# but deliberately allows dot-dirs ("users often want .github/, .claude/").
# That is right for skills and agents and badly wrong for worktrees.

# Agent worktrees are FULL COPIES of this repo created by isolated agent
# sessions. Indexing them made the codebase appear ~4x over: the graph reached
# 378MB with 474,152 references to worktrees/agent-*, which distorts god nodes,
# community detection and every query that leans on them.
#
# Excluded from the graph only — never delete these from disk (see CLAUDE.md:
# "worktree-agent-* branches ... never delete from here").
.claude/worktrees/

# Everything else under .claude/ is kept on purpose: skills/, agents/, rules/
# and workflows/ are hand-authored and genuinely part of how this project works.

# Frozen planning archive + its screenshot/vision-review JSON artifacts.
# Superseded by vault/ (see CLAUDE.md) and pure generated noise.
.planning/**/screenshots/

# Local scratch + build artefacts that carry no architecture.
.next/
graphify-out/

# Bundled build output. `.mastra/output/` is gitignored build product — a single
# minified dist-*.mjs contributing ~3,600 nodes.
#
# Node count understates the damage. A bundle is thousands of tiny, generically
# named functions (get, set, push, parse, call, create) that are densely
# interconnected, so a BFS query seeded on ordinary words lands in the bundle and
# never reaches real code. Before this exclusion, "How does storefront checkout
# create an order and submit it to Printful?" returned 158 nodes, essentially ALL
# of them from dist-CB67HEFG.mjs, and not one line of the actual checkout route.
**/.mastra/
**/dist/
*.min.js
*.bundle.js

# Same failure mode, other sources — found by ranking source files by node count:
#   vault/.obsidian/plugins/obsidian-kanban/main.js   1,033 nodes
#   playwright-report/trace/assets/*.js                 813 nodes
# For scale, the largest REAL source file (lib/db/schema/brain.ts) contributes 77.
# Both are minified: every function is a() / r() / i() at loc=L1.
#
# vault/ itself is deliberately NOT excluded — the domain maps and ADRs are
# exactly the curated knowledge worth having in the graph. Only .obsidian/
# (plugin bundles + editor config) goes.
vault/.obsidian/

# Test/build reports. playwright-report/ and test-results/ are regenerated by
# every e2e run, so they also churn the graph on each rebuild.
playwright-report/
test-results/

# Generated baselines and schema snapshots — machine-written, no architecture.
fallow-baselines/
drizzle/meta/
.file-budget.baseline.json

# Throwaway QA capture dirs. These are per-run screenshot artefacts, not
# architecture, and vision extraction over ~1,300 of them is pure cost.
.qa-tmp-*/
docs/screenshots/
public/screenshots/
audit-verify-*.png
editor-*.png
edit-*.png
